  Copyright (c) 2010 Broadcom Corporation

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Reference brcmsmac sources -- brcmsmac/
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Copied verbatim from the Linux kernel for reference.  Each file retains its
own license header.  All of the bundled files carry the Broadcom per-file ISC
grant quoted above (Copyright (c) 2010 Broadcom Corporation, plus "Copyright
(c) 2013 Hauke Mehrtens" on main.c / mac80211_if.c).  They were written to run
in the GPL-2.0 kernel, so treat them as GPL-on-the-line if you redistribute
them outside this ISC-granted context.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Firmware -- bcm4313_ucode.c / bcm4313_ucode.h / firmware/brcm/bcm43xx-*.fw
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The D11/LCN microcode is a Broadcom binary, redistributable ONLY under the
Broadcom Software License Agreement in firmware/brcm/LICENCE.broadcom_bcm43xx
("Redistributable. See LICENCE.broadcom_bcm43xx for details.", WHENCE entry
for brcmsmac).

Obligations that apply to you if you ship it (including embedded inside the
module in bcm4313_ucode.c):

  - The firmware must be distributed COMPLETE, UNMODIFIED, exactly as
    provided by Broadcom, and only for use with the Broadcom device it was
    designed for.  Do not modify or reverse-engineer the blob (do not strip
    or alter bcm4313_ucode_bin[]/bcm4313_ucode_hdr[]).
  - Distribute it with a copy of the Software License Agreement (kept among
    the sources at firmware/brcm/LICENCE.broadcom_bcm43xx).
  - Keep Broadcom's copyright/trademark notices intact.
  - The firmware is licensed, not sold; title remains with Broadcom.

If you cannot accept these terms, do not include the microcode: the driver
will refuse to attach without it.